## Decisions Made

- **4-wave execution order locked.** Wave 0 = critical fixes (data lies + workflow bugs), Wave 1 = pure noise removal (text density), Wave 2 = layout (drawer width + PA global), Wave 3 = visual redesign (pill / glow / ambient). Each wave has explicit completion criteria. Director called «Для начала уберём просто избыток информации» → noise reduction WITHOUT visual changes is Wave 0+1.
- **Composer fix lives in AssetPreview, not AnimaticPlayer.** Music is a separate layer with its own asset type → composer surface owns its affordances. Rejected option B (extend legacy `/upload-music`) and option C (kebab-only action) in favour of drawer-native upload via NEW route.
- **`/upload-music-direct` is sibling to `/upload-music`, not replacement.** Legacy VID-animatic path stays untouched. Two routes mirror the two asset types music can attach to.
- **Asset status stays REVIEW after Director upload.** Uploaded flag in metadata is informational only — explicit Approve still required. Avoids accidental implicit approval.
- **No route handler integration test added.** Matches project style — only utility/lib tests exist (errors-handler, pipeline-stages, response, status-transitions, storage-probe, ffmpeg-stitch, series-bible, timeline-cell-resolver, vgen-prompt-*, budget, governance). Adding the first route integration test for this fix would be out-of-style.
- **Dev server restart NOT executed unilaterally.** Composer fix is not visible to Director without it, but stopping a parallel-session's dev server could disrupt the Mode 2.5 PA session running in quizzical-brown. Awaiting Director call.

